{"title":"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(Parabola)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (Parabola)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5(guess_with_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5(guess with answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(using_the_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (using the answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(also_calculus_but_more_convoluted)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (also calculus but more convoluted)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(basically_a_more_detailed_version_of_solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (basically a more detailed version of solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the least possible value of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128007ee3b97f3ff741a1e668139edf8c13ba7e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)(x+4)+2019\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"18\" />where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1a975862887a1651ee7e7e41081cd13b698bca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2017 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2018 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 2019 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 2020 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 2021$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"488\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Grouping the first and last terms and two middle terms gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff41d06a0394a796e1cb07aa460c25f9aed7bac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+5x+4)(x^2+5x+6)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" />, which can be simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b4214e4fad59069eb4d7b09da14cbf62a5a6e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+5x+5)^2-1+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"19\" />. Noting that squares are nonnegative, and verifying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb63e6748a6efd487b9add5b2b9de7fdbe150a39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+5x+5=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> for some real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16aa87629fc4d7eb3af83eb24cc6ed75065a72c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28Parabola.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(Parabola)\">Solution 1.1 (Parabola)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (Parabola)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As in Solution 1, we group the first and last terms, and the two middle terms, to obtain:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/406171726484eb974bedb0a517d6ec8efbbd832b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+5x+4)(x^2+5x+6)+2019\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>To clear the algebraic noise and make completing the square straightforward, we can use a variable substitution. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47ffb2de6609575f9a3b619e4db83fb88571e123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^2 + 5x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />. The expression simplifies nicely to a single-variable quadratic:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a1555e2d31a719a74cf08b07383df3122dcdd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y(y + 2) + 2019\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5ca1e5b0beb2d732010f30b4cb3391d96e407ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= y^2 + 2y + 2019\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Now, we can complete the square by adding and subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1dee25a3c20e8e09a29b175285451c09736a6521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (y^2 + 2y + 1) + 2019 - 1\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc4916938fec7bb538a19a86e255bb9a923ee3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (y + 1)^2 + 2018\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e91699d7c6337562efaf03878000ae76eca7dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 5x + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> back in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e296e38a36a40da338564898b1a88015f6a1ff9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\big((x^2 + 5x + 4) + 1\\big)^2 + 2018\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"25\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f21a34bd086cb4456564a7d5a587b0a8f086c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (x^2 + 5x + 5)^2 + 2018\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since any real squared term must be non-negative, the absolute minimum value of the expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16aa87629fc4d7eb3af83eb24cc6ed75065a72c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />. This minimum is strictly achievable because the discriminant of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7d6fc7f14ecc424e7860d72bc5c8dc2b88f823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 5x + 5 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/4/664f872dbc9c5b141c8400dc9af67c39f7b08656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 - 4(1)(5) = 5 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"20\" />, guaranteeing real roots for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 2 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest number that makes this expression minimal is \\( x = -1 \\). This gives 2019, so is the answer 2019? Well, before we jump to conclusions, we need to understand that there may exist a number around or between the interval \\( [-1, 0] \\) such that this number \\( n \\) can make a smaller number. This interval is 1 unit long, so our answer is \\( 2019 - 1 = \\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16aa87629fc4d7eb3af83eb24cc6ed75065a72c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e00c082ea4101184ffffd540eeb8a4c5acf6696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x+\\tfrac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />. Then the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f780f2fc457f3ee899d25ee4de3d4d50dc16966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)(x+4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad07595de90df617bcc661491b8e1c33cd62f0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a-\\tfrac{3}{2}\\right)\\left(a-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(a+\\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(a+\\tfrac{3}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"246\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p>We can now use the difference of two squares to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3dbff21dfae43481821282f812d18ae59b36d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a^2-\\tfrac{9}{4}\\right)\\left(a^2-\\tfrac{1}{4}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"22\" />, and expand this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4eeebb172804d10a60665e194c1740ac06d047c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^4-\\tfrac{5}{2}a^2+\\tfrac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Refactor this by completing the square to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1cab56123c73768d4520f0197e8eb390a15b90a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a^2-\\tfrac{5}{4}\\right)^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />, which has a minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. The answer is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/406210b881ab9728d91ed633e64a4a7d9d0e6123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019-1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"174\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(calculus)\">Solution 4 (calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to Solution 1, grouping the first and last terms and the middle terms, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff41d06a0394a796e1cb07aa460c25f9aed7bac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2+5x+4)(x^2+5x+6)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388ca5bba52221aba8d7304a0b2f75a5b8ad0e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+5x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, we get the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/7754fc5090f105c147b599ec785293f1e80d8cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y+4)(y+6)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we can find the critical points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d24c8cc220cf34f178b7538b8aa2540595a9e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y+4)(y+6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> to minimize the function:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e851893f102bc1346c5e672805b079aad425a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{dy}(y^2+10y+24)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"180\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f1225f44bbe1a454f142f80fc7d6fd3b4fad74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y+10=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eee735a31eb5a6136ac2b801327067ec92040d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y=-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3300f593042c275f64b0c1bfd4ab55315ce3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-5,0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>To minimize the result, we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b18ab3e2e05fad815e6ac2c584f46f0000e905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />. Hence, the minimum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a2d36dba9c4fd85f1b9b47afac4833f8825fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5+4)(-5+6)=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2e57e191b762609d1918cda80912c64fb5086c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1+2019 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"189\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><i>Note</i>: We could also have used the result that minimum/maximum point of a parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878740b1e9bad0008122348eca48d8883a00e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121cd605cf7dc1e301ccc7c17f9ad3cb39ca2c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><i>Note 2:</i> This solution is somewhat \"lucky\", since when we define variables to equal a function, and create another function out of these variables, the domain of such function may vary from the initial one. This is important because the maximum and minimum value of a function is dependent on its domain, e.g:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c484f0e82951283c0f982c105ee57791b7ec70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" /> has no maximum value in the the integers, but once restricting the domain to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00d7e02b5fd0a47f63e7dfcaa68fcb05a6a0a677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Also, observe that if we were to evaluate this by taking the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3b24993efc87646cc0984b8b9651f0793aa764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)(x+4)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"18\" />, we would get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a526e44e36254c196af103613bc724f312b6a209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-value to obtain the minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-value of this expression. It can be seen that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a526e44e36254c196af103613bc724f312b6a209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> is actually an inflection point, instead of a minimum or maximum. \n</p><p>-Note 2 from Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5.28guess_with_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5(guess_with_answer_choices)\">Solution 5(guess with answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5(guess with answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The expression is negative when an odd number of the factors are negative. This happens when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b932a90cc7ffb6506c9fbd8387ab0d6980d8ffb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 &lt; x &lt; -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbe6f71786db0b9ed3d5772dc642a061da22d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-4 &lt; x &lt; -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/08871bd056d487c3b04247df448a348272b97120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\frac32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4f120d9528982e74c3787b5e615070e0a917b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\frac72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/56995bcf0983ffad21eb0aa8a9ac7b1a1b22c8d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{15}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" />, which is very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b9217fc184c777997cdb6ed05e15ee47a080b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 + 2019 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"189\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28using_the_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(using_the_answer_choices)\">Solution 6 (using the answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (using the answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are impossible, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f780f2fc457f3ee899d25ee4de3d4d50dc16966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)(x+4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" /> can be negative (as seen when e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0ac5c35c931930702f526299de31ba8a051754f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" />). Plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0ac5c35c931930702f526299de31ba8a051754f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> to see that it becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79bfd5cfcf3f879c283177d803ccafd2b0422e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019 - \\frac{15}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />, so round this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d65331bb23df63d88bdf3bd414ec65a7b6e4492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"83\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>We can also see that the limit of the function is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> since at the minimum, two of the numbers are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but two are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28also_calculus_but_more_convoluted.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(also_calculus_but_more_convoluted)\">Solution 7 (also calculus but more convoluted)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (also calculus but more convoluted)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can ignore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49e1f42131f302f2b4a45393cdc3fed5be2655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and consider it later, as it is a constant. By difference of squares, we can group this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca8b9cd3ee81d33ed5ffe0fb52c57705a2c5746c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left((x+2.5)^2-0.5^2\\right)\\left((x+2.5)^2-1.5^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"298\" height=\"23\" />. We pull a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> into each term to avoid dealing with decimals: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a91c163931525913ebf4694b7ca64a3e33b753.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\left((2x+5)^2-1\\right)\\left((2x+5)^2-9\\right)}{16}.\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Now, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e60322bbb329c4427499cb9cc885cb4bfefbec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2x+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />. Our expression becomes: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f4ed45ff3ad77fab943299d679c17a13d85b3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{(a-1)(a-9)}{16}=\\dfrac{a^2-10a+9}{16}.\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Taking the derivative, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6da88960116f63b11e6c9c5191717271518b9008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2a-10}{16}=\\dfrac{a-5}8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"38\" /> This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53897e4b47f6049266b4bffcef91bc949385b5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53897e4b47f6049266b4bffcef91bc949385b5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we get the expression is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and therefore our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06de98db63fd88674eba3a43ef95099cae367a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2019-1=\\boxed{\\text{(B)}~2018}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28basically_a_more_detailed_version_of_solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(basically_a_more_detailed_version_of_solution_1)\">Solution 8 (basically a more detailed version of solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (basically a more detailed version of solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f780f2fc457f3ee899d25ee4de3d4d50dc16966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)(x+4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" /> can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61ba425713f9fd34ff0e6b479d875e8a2332739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(x+1)(x+4)][(x+2)(x+3)]=(x^2+5x+4)(x^2+5x+6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"480\" height=\"21\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e02ff11f6560e123b7b58d3ef31bf98e18c594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x^2+5x+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5b78f17f72db72a25f8553d055ec4176a329495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)(a+1)=a^2 -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Then the whole problem can be written as the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d6e9a8b3e026863efa125ecb71332d1a88bdd95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^2 -1)+2019$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d56e958b2ac8b3b4cac113efc25e52982fa15b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a^2)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336ba9e4d8b9bcb827d5485e09f83bf8d67283f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 +5x+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> has at least one real root, which we can verify with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd0100979d4f7992e58423b867dca05b5a5e6c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b^2-4ac) \\to (5^2)-(4 \\times 1 \\times 5)=5 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" />. \nThus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c43e0d5000e873385ed38efe11a1695ee49404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0-1)+2019= \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"222\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~pandapower24\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vf2LkM7ExhY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vf2LkM7ExhY</a> by SpreadTheMathLove\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lis8yKT9WXc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lis8yKT9WXc</a> (less than 2 minutes)\n</p>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NRa3VnjNVbw\">https://youtu.be/NRa3VnjNVbw</a> - Education, the Study of Everything</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mfa7j2BoNjI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mfa7j2BoNjI</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tIzJtgJbHGc\">https://youtu.be/tIzJtgJbHGc</a> - savannahsolver</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3dfbWzOfJAI?t=3319\">https://youtu.be/3dfbWzOfJAI?t=3319</a> - pi_is_3.14</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t=1134\">https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t=1134</a> ~ pi_is_3.14</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/q-80GjQeWes\">https://youtu.be/q-80GjQeWes</a> (timestamp: 21:03) - Claire Wang</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margi